The modes of procurement under RA 12009 are: [E1]

a) Competitive Bidding;  
b) Limited Source Bidding; [E1]
c) Competitive Dialogue;  
d) Unsolicited Offer with Bid Matching; [E1]
e) Direct Contracting;  
f) Direct Acquisition;  
g) Repeat Order;  
h) Small Value Procurement; [E1]
i) Negotiated Procurement;  
j) Direct Sales; and  
k) Direct Procurement for Science, Technology and Innovation [E1].

These modes are adopted consistent with the fit-for-purpose procurement approach, and detailed procedures for each mode are provided in the IRR and manuals issued by the GPPB [E1], [E6].
